            <!-- API DOCS -->
            <div class="panel" id="panel-docs">
                <div style="font-size:18px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px">API Documentation</div>
                <div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--fg2);margin-bottom:16px">Static JSON API exposing every dump published on this site. No auth, no rate limit, CORS enabled — point any HTTP client at the files.</div>

                <div class="docs-note">
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">Base URL</b><br>
                    Production: <code>https://deko661.github.io/hwidr-dump-site/api/</code><br>
                    Local: <code>site/local/api/</code> (works over <code>file://</code>)<br>
                    <br>
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">All paths below are relative to the Base URL</b>. Every game has its own folder: <code>/api/fortnite/</code>, <code>/api/valorant/</code>, <code>/api/apex/</code>, <code>/api/roblox/</code>. There are <b>no</b> endpoints at the bare <code>/api/</code> root — you must always include the game name.<br>
                    <br>
                    <b style="color:var(--fg)">sdkContent.json</b> is split into parts for hosting size limits: fetch <code>sdkContent.json.part0</code> … <code>partN</code>, <code>JSON.parse</code> each part (each is a valid <code>{"Category/Name": "header"}</code> object) and merge with <code>Object.assign</code>.
                </div>

                <div style="margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:600">Endpoints</div>
                <div id="docs-endpoints"></div>

                <div style="margin:24px 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:600">Examples</div>
                <div class="code-block" style="margin-bottom:12px">
                    <div class="header">JavaScript — read Fortnite GWorld offset</div>
                    <pre>fetch('https://deko661.github.io/hwidr-dump-site/api/fortnite/offsets.json')
  .then(r =&gt; r.json())
  .then(data =&gt; {
    const gw = data.namespaces.Offsets.GWorld;   // "0x1c8e1578"
    console.log('GWorld =', gw);
  });</pre>
                </div>
                <div class="code-block" style="margin-bottom:12px">
                    <div class="header">Python — search Valorant names for "BP_"</div>
                    <pre>import json, urllib.request

url = 'https://deko661.github.io/hwidr-dump-site/api/valorant/names.json'
names = json.load(urllib.request.urlopen(url))
hits = [n for n in names if 'BP_' in n['name']]
print(len(hits), 'blueprint names')</pre>
                </div>
                <div class="code-block" style="margin-bottom:16px">
                    <div class="header">C++ — consume Fortnite offsets directly</div>
                    <pre>// data.namespaces.Offsets maps 1:1 with the raw Offsets.hpp
#include &lt;cstdint&gt;

struct Offsets {
    uint32_t GWorld = 0x1c8e1578; // from api/fortnite/offsets.json
};</pre>
                </div>

                <div style="margin:24px 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:600">Field reference — shapes returned by each endpoint</div>
                <table class="dump-table" style="font-size:11px">
                    <thead><tr><th style="width:30%">Endpoint</th><th>Shape</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody id="docs-fields"></tbody>
                </table>

                <div style="margin:24px 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:600">Copy-paste for an AI</div>
                <div class="docs-note" style="font-size:11px">
                    <code style="font-size:10px">HWIDR SDK Viewer static JSON API.<br>
Base URL: https://deko661.github.io/hwidr-dump-site/api/ (or site/local/api/ locally).<br>
All endpoints are under /api/{game}/ where {game} is one of: fortnite, valorant, apex.<br>
No auth, no rate limit, CORS enabled.<br>
<br>
Endpoints per game:<br>
- {game}/manifest.json — API metadata, games list, endpoint index, counts<br>
- {game}/offsets.json — {"namespaces": {"Offsets": {"GWorld": "0x..."}}, "rawOffsetsHpp": "..."}<br>
- {game}/decrypts.json — {"files": {"file.hpp": {"Namespace": [{"name": "X", "value": "0x...", "type": "uint32_t"}]}}, "rawHeaders": {...}}<br>
- {game}/names.json — [{"index": 0, "name": "ObjectRedirector"}, ...]<br>
- {game}/objects.json — [{"index": 0, "type": "Class", "name": "/Script/Engine.Engine"}, ...]<br>
- {game}/typeCounts.json — {"Class": 12345, "Function": 6789, ...}<br>
- {game}/functions.json — {"ClassName": [{"name": "Foo", "offset": "0x..."}], ...} (empty {} for Fortnite)<br>
- {game}/sdk.json — {"Classes": ["AActor", ...], "Structs": [...], "Enums": [...]} (names only)<br>
- {game}/sdkContent.json.part0 … partN — {"Category/Name": "// header source ...", ...} (split into parts, merge with Object.assign)<br>
- apex/apex.json — {"mics": [[name, 0x..]...], "buttons": [...], "recvTables": {"table": [[field, 0x..]...]}, "convars": [...], "stats": {...}}<br>
<br>
Example: GET https://deko661.github.io/hwidr-dump-site/api/fortnite/offsets.json then read data.namespaces.Offsets.GWorld.</code>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- OFFSETS -->
